---

---
<details open>
	<summary>
		<h2 id="inline-elements">Inline Text Elements</h2>
	</summary>

	<section>
		<h3 id="a">Links (<code>&lt;a&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p>Visited link: <a href="/styleguide/">This Page</a></p>
		<p>Not visited link: <a href="#" id="random-link" rel="nofollow">Random Error Page</a></p>
		<script type="module" is:inline>
			(/** @type {HTMLAnchorElement} */ (document.querySelector('#random-link'))).href = crypto.randomUUID();
		</script>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="abbr-dfn">Abbreviation & Inline Definition (<code>&lt;abbr&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;dfn&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p>
			The term "<dfn><abbr title="Situation Normal, All Fucked Up">SNAFU</abbr></dfn>", meaning "Situation Normal, All Fucked Up", originates from <abbr title="World War II"
			>WW2</abbr> military slang.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="strong-b">Strong &amp; Bold (<code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;b&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p>Whiskey is a <strong>strong</strong> drink, while wine can be <b>bold</b>.</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="em-i">Emphasis &amp; Italic (<code>&lt;em&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;i&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p><i>Italics</i> is a form of <em>emphasize</em> text.</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="sub-sup-small">Size &amp; Position (<code>&lt;sub&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;sup&gt;</code>, &amp; <code>&lt;small&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p>Like on rollercoasters, we can go <sup>up</sup>, <sub>down</sub>, or feel <small>tiny</small>.</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="cite-q">Inline Quotes &amp; Citations (<code>&lt;cite&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;q&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p>
			As best said by the Cheshire Cat in <cite><a
					href="https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/19033"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
				>Alice's Adventure in Wonderland</a></cite>:
			<q>If you don't know where you are going any road can take you there.</q>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="mark-del-ins">
			Highlights &amp; Annotations (<code>&lt;mark&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;del&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;ins&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;u&gt;</code>, &amp; <code>&lt;s&gt;</code>)
		</h3>

		<p>One of the <mark>highlights</mark> of marking text is that you can indicate <u>typos</u> and <s>cleverness</s> sarcasm.</p>

		<p>Or even, text <del>deletions</del><ins>insertions</ins>.</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="code">Computer text (<code>&lt;code&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;kbd&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;var&gt;</code>, &amp; <code>&lt;samp&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p>You can <code>type</code> all you like, even try to <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> my <var>vars</var>, but all they say is:</p>
		<p><samp>Null Pointer Exception.</samp></p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="data-time">Machine readable markup (<code>&lt;data&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;time&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p><data value="42">The Answer to the Ultimate Question of Life, the Universe, and Everything</data></p>

		<p>Current date and time: <time datetime="" id="cur-time">&mdash;</time></p>
		<script type="module" is:inline>
			const curTimeElement = /** @type {HTMLTimeElement} */ (document.querySelector('#cur-time'));

			setInterval(() => {
				const now = new Date();

				curTimeElement.dateTime = now.toISOString();
				curTimeElement.innerText = now.toLocaleString();
				// oxlint-disable-next-line no-magic-numbers
			}, 1000);
		</script>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="br-span-wbr-bdo-bdi">
			Breaks & Text Direction (<code>&lt;br&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;span&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;wbr&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;bdo&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;bdi&gt;</code>)
		</h3>

		<p>
			Here is a line break:
			<br />
			That's it.
		</p>

		<p>Here is a <span>span of text</span>.</p>

		<p>Here is a super long word in a tiny space just for the sake of having word break opportunities:</p>
		<p style="max-inline-size: var(--size-content-0); outline: solid thin var(--theme-color)">
			pneumono<wbr />ultra<wbr />microscopic<wbr />silico<wbr />volcano<wbr />coniosis
		</p>

		<p>Here is some text intentionally right-to-left:</p>
		<p>
			The Hebrew word "<bdo dir="rtl">שָׁלוֹם</bdo>" (Shalom) and the Arabic word "<bdi>سَلَام</bdi>" (Salām) share the same etymologic root. Both have a
			literal meaning of "peace".
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h3 id="ruby-rp-rt">Ruby Text (<code>&lt;ruby&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;rp&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;rt&gt;</code>)</h3>

		<p>
			Ruby text is a type of annotation to help understanding the meaning of text.
		</p>
		<p>
			In Japanese, this text is know as "<span lang="ja"><ruby>振<rp>(</rp><rt>ふ</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><span>り</span><ruby>仮<rp>
						(
					</rp><rt>が</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby><ruby>名<rp>(</rp><rt>な</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby></span>" (Furigana).
		</p>
	</section>
</details>
